<div id="formulaPop" class="popup"><button onclick="closePop('formulaPop')">Close</button><h3>Formula Sheet - SMS 3163</h3><p><b>Simple:</b> I = P x r x t, A = P(1 + r t) | <b>Compound:</b> A = P(1 + i)^n, PV = A / (1 + i)^n | <b>Discount:</b> v = 1 / (1 + i) | <b>Annuity-immediate:</b> a-angle-n = (1 - v^n) / i | <b>Annuity-due:</b> a-double-dot = (1 - v^n) / d | <b>Accumulated:</b> s-angle-n = ((1 + i)^n - 1) / i | <b>Nominal:</b> i^(m) / m per period, Effective: (1 + i^(m)/m)^m - 1 | <b>Loan:</b> Payment = Loan / a-angle-n</p></div>
<div id="glossPop" class="popup"><button onclick="closePop('glossPop')">Close</button><h3>Glossary - SMS 3163</h3><p><b>Interest:</b> price of money over time. <b>Principal:</b> starting amount. <b>Accumulated value:</b> value in future. <b>Present value:</b> value today. <b>Discount factor:</b> v = 1 / (1 + i). <b>Annuity:</b> series of level payments. <b>Annuity-immediate:</b> payments at end of period. <b>Annuity-due:</b> payments at start. <b>Amortisation:</b> paying loan by instalments. <b>Yield:</b> return earned. <b>Nominal rate:</b> quoted rate with frequency. <b>Effective rate:</b> true yearly rate.</p></div>
<div class="topic active" id="topic1">
<h2>Topic 1: Simple and Compound Interest</h2><p><b>Estimated time:</b> ~35 minutes | <b>Objectives:</b> Distinguish simple vs compound, calculate interest and amount, explain why compound grows faster.</p>
<p>Simple interest only pays on the original principal. Compound interest pays on principal + interest already earned. That is why compound grows faster.</p><div class='keybox'><p><b>Simple:</b> I = P x r x t. Example: P=10000, r=10%, t=2. I = 10000 x 0.10 x 2 = 2000. A = 12000.</p><p><b>Compound:</b> A = P(1+i)^n. Example: P=10000, i=10%, n=2. A = 10000 x 1.10^2 = 12100. Interest = 2100.</p><p><b>Rule:</b> Always convert % to decimal: 10% = 0.10. Always check n = years, not months, unless told.</p></div>
