<div class="topic" id="topic2">
<h2>Topic 2: Discount, Present Value and Accumulated Value</h2><p><b>Estimated time:</b> ~35 minutes | <b>Objectives:</b> Explain discount factor, calculate PV and AV, explain time value.</p>
<p>Present value is how much future money is worth today. Accumulated value is how much today's money will be worth in future.</p><div class='keybox'><p><b>Discount factor:</b> v = 1 / (1+i). If i=10%, v = 1/1.10 = 0.9091.</p><p><b>PV:</b> PV = Future x v^n. Example: 12100 in 2 years at 10%: PV = 12100 x 0.9091^2 = 12100 x 0.8264 = 10000.</p><p><b>AV:</b> AV = Present x (1+i)^n. Example: 10000 today, 10%, 2 years: AV = 12100.</p></div><p><b>Time value:</b> 10000 today is better than 10000 in a year, because you can invest it.</p>
