<div class="topic" id="topic3">
<h2>Topic 3: Annuities - Level Payments</h2><p><b>Estimated time:</b> ~40 minutes | <b>Objectives:</b> Explain annuity-immediate and annuity-due, calculate PV and AV of annuity, choose correct formula.</p>
<p>An annuity is a series of equal payments, e.g. rent every month, pension every year.</p><div class='keybox'><p><b>Annuity-immediate:</b> Payments at END of each period. PV = Payment x a-angle-n, where a-angle-n = (1 - v^n)/i.</p><p><b>Annuity-due:</b> Payments at START of each period. PV = Payment x a-double-dot-angle-n, where a-double-dot = (1 - v^n)/d, d = i/(1+i).</p><p><b>Example:</b> Pay 10000 at end of each year for 3 years, i=10%. v=0.9091. a-angle-3 = (1 - 0.7513)/0.10 = 2.4869. PV = 10000 x 2.4869 = 24869.</p></div><p><b>Exam trick:</b> Read 'at beginning' vs 'at end'. That one word changes the formula.</p>
