<h2>Topic 4: Loans and Amortisation</h2><p><b>Estimated time:</b> ~35 minutes | <b>Objectives:</b> Explain loan repayment, calculate instalment, split interest vs capital, build amortisation table.</p>
<p>A loan is repaid by equal instalments. Each instalment = interest on outstanding loan + part of capital. Early payments are mostly interest. Later payments are mostly capital.</p><div class='keybox'><p><b>Instalment:</b> Payment = Loan / a-angle-n.</p><p><b>Example:</b> Loan 100000, i=10%, n=3. a-angle-3 = 2.4869. Payment = 100000 / 2.4869 = 40211.48.</p><p><b>Year 1:</b> Interest = 100000 x 10% = 10000. Capital = 40211.48 - 10000 = 30211.48. Outstanding = 69788.52.</p></div>
