<h2>Topic 5: Bonds, Yields and Project Appraisal</h2><p><b>Estimated time:</b> ~35 minutes | <b>Objectives:</b> Explain bond, calculate price, explain yield, explain NPV and IRR for projects.</p>
<p>A bond is a loan to a company / government. You pay price today, you receive coupons (interest) + redemption (principal) later.</p><div class='keybox'><p><b>Bond price:</b> PV of coupons + PV of redemption.</p><p><b>Yield:</b> Return you actually earn. If price falls, yield rises.</p><p><b>NPV:</b> PV of inflows - Cost. If NPV > 0, accept. If NPV < 0, reject.</p><p><b>IRR:</b> Rate where NPV = 0. If IRR > cost of capital, accept.</p></div>
