<h2>Topic 6: Nominal vs Effective Rates and Inflation</h2><p><b>Estimated time:</b> ~30 minutes | <b>Objectives:</b> Distinguish nominal vs effective, convert, adjust for inflation, explain real rate.</p>
<p>Nominal rate is quoted. Effective rate is what you actually earn in a year. If interest is paid monthly, effective > nominal, because you earn interest on interest within the year.</p><div class='keybox'><p><b>Convert:</b> Effective = (1 + i^(m)/m)^m - 1. Example: Nominal 12% convertible monthly: Monthly = 1%. Effective = 1.01^12 - 1 = 12.68%.</p><p><b>Real rate:</b> If nominal is 10% and inflation is 4%, real is about 6%. Exact: (1.10/1.04) - 1 = 5.77%.</p></div>
